---
model: claude
prompt:
  schemaStrictness: retry
permissions:
  # A plan run is read-only investigation, so it states its whole posture here
  # rather than leaving it to Go: an unstated posture is filled in with the edit
  # preset and the full edit toolset, which is the opposite of what plan means.
  # The plan file itself is written by the agent's native plan mode, not by a
  # Write call (todos/plans.go: "gavel never writes it").
  mode: plan
  tools:
    Read: allow
    Glob: allow
    Grep: allow
---
{{#if multiple}}You are planning the implementation of the {{count}} todo items listed below. Produce ONE plan that covers all of them.{{else}}You are planning the implementation of the todo item below in this codebase.{{/if}}

{{{body}}}---
## Instructions

You are running in your native plan mode: investigate the codebase (read-only) and author a complete implementation plan in your plan-mode plan file. Do NOT modify any source files.

1. Explore the code paths the todo touches; understand the root cause or design before planning.
2. Write a step-by-step implementation plan into your plan file: the files to change, new types/functions and their signatures, what gets deleted, the testing strategy, and risks.
3. Report the plan file's ABSOLUTE path in the final StructuredOutput call's top-level `planPath` field — gavel records it on the todo and renders the plan from that file for human review.
{{#if existingPlan}}
4. An earlier plan for this todo already exists (below). Re-evaluate it against the current code: if it still stands as written, report top-level `planStatus` "unchanged" (no rewrite needed); if it needs revision, write the revised plan and report `planStatus` "updated".

## Existing Plan

{{{existingPlan}}}
{{else}}
4. This todo has no prior plan; author one and report top-level `planStatus` "new".
{{/if}}

The final StructuredOutput call carries `summary`, `endStatus`, `planStatus`, and `planPath` (or `planContent`) as separate top-level fields. Never JSON-encode an object or another field value into a string.

If you are blocked on a decision only a human can make, stop and report endStatus "ask" with your questions in the final result instead of guessing.
